From 80272b433e138ef3a2274079685023b9d4bfaf30 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rudi Heitbaum <rudi@heitbaum.com>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 12:57:17 +1000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: rockchip: rk3399pro-vmarc-som: add i2c2 scl
 timing

The hym8563 on i2c2 does not ack:

  rtc-hym8563 2-0051: could not init device, -6

It is also the ext_clock for sdio-pwrseq, so wifi does not come up
either.

i2c2 runs at 400 kHz with no scl edge times. The core defaults both to
300 ns and rk3x-i2c derives the high period from

  min_high_ns = scl_rise_ns + 600

giving 900 ns, which is short for this bus. It acks at 100 kHz.

Set the edges to the values i2c3 already uses, giving 1050 ns at
400 kHz.

Tested on a Radxa ROCK Pi N10: rtc0 registers and keeps time across a
reboot, the sdio card enumerates at SDR104 and wlan0 appears.
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3399pro-vmarc-som.dtsi | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3399pro-vmarc-som.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3399pro-vmarc-som.dtsi
index 64e6ba3..074f09c 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3399pro-vmarc-som.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3399pro-vmarc-som.dtsi
@@ -296,6 +296,8 @@
 
 &i2c2 {
 	clock-frequency = <400000>;
+	i2c-scl-falling-time-ns = <15>;
+	i2c-scl-rising-time-ns = <450>;
 	status = "okay";
 
 	hym8563: rtc@51 {
